  "texts": {
    "preamble": "The Food Safety Officer vs Basil P.Mathew on 19 November, 2019 Author: Ashok Menon Bench: Ashok Menon In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice Ashok Menon Tuesday, The 19Th Day Of November 2019 / 28Th Karthika, 1941 Crl.L.P..No.429 Of 2019 Against The Order/Judgment In Cc 469/2017 Dated 22-04-2019 Of Jmfc, Kakkanad (Temporary) Petitioner/Complainant: The Food Safety Officer, Thrikkakkara Circle,Ernakulam District,Represented By The Public Prosecutor,High Court Of Kerala, Ernakulam. By Sri C. S Hrithwik, Sr Pp Respondents/Accused: 1 Basil P.Mathew Food Business Operator,S/O.P.C.Mathew, Parakkal House, Thuruthussery, Maikkad.P.O, (Manager M/S.Priyom Mega Mart)-683589. 2 Issac George, Maliakkal House, Kunnathunad, Kumarapuram.P.O,(D And O Licensee Of M/S.Priyom Mega Mart), Pin -690548. 3 M/S.Priyom Mega Mart Llp, 3/947-Gh,Smart Centre, Civil Lane Road, Vazhakkala, Thrikkakara.P.O, Kakkanad, (Represented By A2), Pin - 682021. 4 P X Johny, Spick And Span Marketing, Kalika Ganapathy The Food Safety Officer vs Basil P.Mathew on 19 November, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/170858173/ 1 Temple Road, Vaduthala, Kochi-23 (Responsible Person Of Spick And Spam Marketing). Crl.LP 429/2019 2 5 M/S.Spick And Spam Marketing, Kalika Ganapathy Temple Road, Vaduthala, Kochi-23(Represented By 4). 6 P.Murugesan, S/O Palaniyandi, No.4, Bharathiyar Street 2Nd Cross, Thiruchirappalli-620002 (Nominee Of M/S.Lion Dates Impex Private Limited). 7 M/S.Lion Dates Impex Private Limited, 27/3 Cauvery Road, Trichy-620002 (Represented By Its Nominee A6). R1-7 By Adv. Sri.Santhosh Subramanian R1-7 By Adv. Sri.E.A.Thankappan R1-7 By Adv. Sri.Sherry J. Thomas R1-7 By Adv. Sri.S.Sreekumar(North Paravur) R1-7 By Adv. Sri.Joemon Antony Other Present: Sri C. S Hrithwik Sr Pp This Criminal Leave Petition Having Been Finally Heard On 19.11.2019 , The Court On The Same Day Passed The Following: Crl.LP 429/2019 3 O R D E R",
    "facts": "It is true that the case was posted for hearing the complaint. But the observation of the learned Magistrate that the complainant has never appeared, does not appear to be true from the copy of the proceedings, which is produced before this Court. From 23.3.2019, the complainant was absent and thereafter, the case was posted for hearing on three dates and he could not appear.",
